  <p>Module revision {radio.revision} · Air–ground voice radio for pilots: how to transmit, how to say letters and numbers, how to make and answer calls, and what to do in an emergency or when the radio fails. Written for military pilots: US Navy training practice first (a training squadron's sortie calls, formation check-ins and training-rule calls), then the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) rules that every military aircraft follows in US airspace.</p>
