  <p class="fig-caption">The first two situations are from the VT-10 script; the third and fourth are the AIM's examples; the last is constructed. The script's ground call has no position element; away from home field, add your position on the airport surface as the AIM asks.</p>
 </section>

 <h2 id="words">Words that do the work</h2>
 <p>A few procedure words carry precise meanings. Using the right one saves a transmission; using the wrong one can mislead. <strong>Roger</strong> means only that you received the whole transmission: it must not answer a yes-or-no question. <a href="#source-pcg">{g('ROGER')}</a></p>
 <dl class="jargon">
  <div><dt>Roger</dt><dd>I have received all of your last transmission. Not an answer to a question needing a yes or no.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Wilco</dt><dd>I have received your message, understand it, and will comply with it.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Affirmative</dt><dd>Yes.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Negative</dt><dd>No; or permission not granted; or that is not correct.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Unable</dt><dd>Indicates inability to comply with a specific instruction, request or clearance.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Say again</dt><dd>Used to request a repeat of the last transmission.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>I say again</dt><dd>The message will be repeated.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Stand by</dt><dd>The controller or pilot must pause for a few seconds, usually to attend to other duties of a higher priority.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Read back</dt><dd>Repeat my message back to me.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Verify</dt><dd>Request confirmation of information, e.g. "verify assigned altitude".</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Acknowledge</dt><dd>Let me know that you have received and understood this message.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Advise intentions</dt><dd>Tell me what you plan to do.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Immediately</dt><dd>Compliance is required to avoid an imminent situation.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Negative contact</dt><dd>Previously issued traffic is not in sight; or you were unable to contact ATC on a particular frequency.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Words twice</dt><dd>Communication is difficult: please say every phrase twice; or, every phrase in this message will be spoken twice.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Speak slower</dt><dd>A request to reduce speech rate.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Over</dt><dd>My transmission is ended; I expect a response.</dd></div>
  <div><dt>Out</dt><dd>The conversation is ended and no response is expected.</dd></div>
 </dl>
 <p class="fig-caption">Definitions from the Pilot/Controller Glossary. <a href="#source-pcg">{g('entries as listed')}</a></p>
