 </section>

 <h2 id="nordo">When the radio fails</h2>
 <h3>At a towered airport</h3>
 <p>Arriving with the <strong>receiver</strong> inoperative, remain outside or above the Class D surface area until you have determined the direction and flow of traffic, then advise the tower of your aircraft type, position, altitude and intention to land, and request light signals. About 3 to 5 miles out, advise your position and join the traffic pattern, watching the tower for light signals. With the <strong>transmitter</strong> inoperative, monitor the tower frequency, and acknowledge tower transmissions or light signals by rocking your wings in daylight, or by blinking the landing or navigation lights at night. <a href="#source-aim">{a('4-2-13')}</a></p>
